                "source": "Buffer",
                "text": "I'm excited to announce this year's IL-11 Congressional App Challenge winners!\n\nCongratulations to the first-place winner, Ishaanvi Vemula from Metea Valley High School! Her app, \"InsureLit,\" simplifies health coverage by making insurance terms easy to understand. It scans insurance documents using OCR, decodes complex terms into plain language, and provides tailored health resources for users. \n\nIn second place is Harish Ramasubramanian, also from Metea Valley High School, with his app, \"AdmitLens.\" Kalyan Cherukuri and Aardarsh Sivaraman from IMSA came in third with their app, \"Echo.\"\n\nCongratulations to all the finalists and everyone who submitted an app! Each year, I'm impressed with the bright students in our district; the future is in good hands!",
